From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:58:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 059/342] meson_hdmi: HDMI audio, 48 kHz 16-bit stereo, as a
 multi_audio device

The display driver publishes audio/hmulti/meson_hdmi/1 next to the
display. The path: a ring of two 1024-frame buffers, read by the AIU's
I2S DMA, the AIU's I2S encoder, the HDMI TX's I2S input, the DesignWare
controller's audio sampler; MPLL2 at 294.912 MHz gives cts_amclk =
12.288 MHz (256 fs) and a 64 fs bit clock, which is also the controller's
master clock. N is 6144; the controller measures CTS.

The client (the media_server's multi_audio node) writes the ring
directly through a write combining mapping in its team. A 2 ms timer
watches the DMA's read pointer and ends buffer exchanges (all SPIs are
level in the GIC driver, the AIU's interrupt is an edge); a buffer's
start time is back-dated by how far the DMA is into it.

Found on the board with an HDMI capture stick:
* the I2S core encodes 24-bit samples: a 16-bit one goes to the top
  ("MSB position" 2) with 16-bit words MSB first, else the controller
  got its upper byte as the lower one;
* the DMA's end pointer is the start of the last 256-byte block, else it
  ran on past the ring;
* the LRCLK divider (64 bit clocks), both clocks inverted, skew 1;
* the encoder is released and reset once the DMA has filled its FIFO,
  else the channel order is undefined (they also need swapping back);
* the controller's I2S part is reset once the I2S clock runs, and CTS is
  then checked against the pixel clock (for N 6144 at 48 kHz, CTS is the
  pixel clock in kHz), again after every mode set: it measures once, and
  a wrong CTS makes the sink play at a wrong rate. The audio clocks are
  set up at attach.

Kernel debugger: "meson_hdmi audio [tone | stop | aiu <word> [<value>]]",
"meson_hdmi dw|top|hhi <register> [<value>]".

Tested: a test tone and the multi_audio path (a buffer-aligned tone, 10 s
without a discontinuity), MediaPlayer through the media_server (440 Hz
left, 660 Hz right, complete channel separation, no gaps in 15 s), mode
changes between 1080p60 and 720p60 while playing (CTS 148501 and 74251).

Sources: S905 datasheet (AIU, audio clocks), S905X datasheet (HDMITX
top), NetBSD dw_hdmi.c (BSD-2); facts only from Linux (cts_amclk mux
values, the AIU sequence and register values named above).

